<title>SOUTH AFRICA: SAfrica's HL&amp;H cuts back head office role.</title>
<headline>SAfrica's HL&amp;H cuts back head office role.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's food and timber holding group Hunt Leuchars &amp; Hepburn Holdings Ltd said on Friday that it was cutting the role of its corporate office following the retirement of group chief executive Neil Morris at the end of March.</p>
<p>The firm said that the responsibility for group operations would now reside principally with the individual units' boards.</p>
<p>The group board will now play a monitoring role and the corporate office will be focused on administration under the management of Brian de Klerk.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
